# Keep host build output out of the image build context.
#
# This is not an optimisation. `COPY src/ src/` runs after the restore layer, so a host `obj/`
# directory overwrites the container's restore output — and `project.assets.json` records absolute
# package paths, which on this host are Windows paths under C:\Users. The build then fails with
# NETSDK1064 "package was not found", naming a package that is present in the offline feed, because
# it is looking for it somewhere that does not exist inside the container.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Never bake local overrides or credentials into an image.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/*.user
**/secrets.json

# Not part of any build.
.git/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
references/
docs/
k8s/
**/TestResults/
**/*.md
